# Face and QR Graudate Scan Flask Application

A Face and QR Graudate system supporting multiple algorithms including HOG + Dlib, DeepFace, InsightFace, and MTCNN + FaceNet. Features include QR code scanning, text-to-speech, and email notifications.

## Features

- 🎯 Multiple face recognition algorithms (HOG + Dlib, DeepFace, InsightFace, MTCNN + FaceNet)
- 📷 Real-time camera-based face detection
- 📱 QR code scanning support
- 🔊 Text-to-speech notifications
- 📧 Email notification system
- 🎓 Student database management

## Prerequisites

- **Python 3.8.8** (recommended)
- **Git** installed on your system
- **CMake** and **Visual Studio Build Tools** (for dlib compilation)

## Installation

### 1. Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone <your-repo-url>
cd reasearch_face-flusk_basic
```

### 2. Create and Activate Virtual Environment

```bash
# Create virtual environment
python -m venv venv

# Activate virtual environment
# Windows (PowerShell)
.\venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1

# Windows (CMD)
.\venv\Scripts\activate.bat

# Linux/Mac
source venv/bin/activate
```

### 3. Install dlib Dependencies

Follow the guide: [How to Install Face Recognition in Python on Windows](https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/installation-guide/how-to-install-face-recognition-in-python-on-windows/)

### 4. Install Python Dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### 5. Troubleshooting InsightFace Installation

If you encounter issues with InsightFace, install manually from the provided wheel:

```bash
pip install installation_tools/insightface-0.7.3-cp310-cp310-win_amd64.whl
```

## Usage

### Run the Application

```bash
python app.py
```

The application will start a Flask server. Open your browser and navigate to:
```
http://localhost:5000
```

## Project Structure

```
reasearch_face-flusk_basic/
├── app.py                          # Main Flask application
├── requirements.txt                # Python dependencies
├── train.ipynb                     # Training notebook for face encodings
├── data/
│   ├── student_list.csv            # Student database
│   ├── encodings/                  # Pre-trained face encodings
│   ├── Image/                      # Student images
│   ├── qr_codes/                   # Generated QR codes
│   └── test_set/                   # Test images
├── img_processing_class/
│   ├── fr_algorithm_class/         # Face recognition algorithms
│   │   ├── fr_deepface.py
│   │   ├── fr_hog_dlib.py
│   │   ├── fr_insightface.py
│   │   └── fr_mtcnn_facenet.py
│   └── utility_class/              # Utility modules
│       ├── adaptive_preprocessor.py
│       ├── box_helper.py
│       ├── camera.py
│       ├── email_sender.py
│       ├── qr_code_scanner.py
│       ├── student_database.py
│       └── text_to_speach.py
├── installation_tools/             # Manual installation files
├── static/                         # CSS and JavaScript files
└── templates/                      # HTML templates
```

## Supported Face Recognition Algorithms

| Algorithm | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| HOG + Dlib | Histogram of Oriented Gradients with Dlib |
| DeepFace | Deep learning-based (Facenet512 + RetinaFace) |
| InsightFace | Buffalo model for face recognition |
| MTCNN + FaceNet | Multi-task CNN with FaceNet embeddings |

## Notes

- Ensure your webcam is connected and accessible
- Face encodings must be generated before running recognition (use `train.ipynb`)
- Adjust confidence/threshold values in `app.py` for better accuracy

